{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962274,"nonce":"Ng1mRh0sGzaLL7dbrqAMxWn9Z3A=","title":"Signals and deriveds can never be disposed","message":"ReactiveGraph removes effects (dispose_effect, reactive.rs:757) but has no\nway to remove a signal or a derived, so every one ever created stays in the\ngraph's slotmaps for the life of the process, along with every\nPropertyBindingRegistry entry bound to it. An embedder that creates signals\nper component leaks them all. Measured through ashui on stock HashLink 1.15\n(Linux x86_64): about 6 MB of RSS per 50k signals, growing linearly; the\nhandles themselves are freed.\n\nWhat references the ids:\n- SignalId: graph.signals; dependencies of each derived and effect in its\n  subscribers; graph.tracking mid-compute; PropertyBindingRegistry.bindings\n  and by_node (binding.rs:526-539); STATEFUL_DEPS (stateful.rs:721-723);\n  HookState.signals for keyed hooks (context_state.rs:85).\n- DerivedId: graph.derived; SubscriberId::Derived in its dependencies'\n  subscribers; derived_dirty_buffer; derived_bindings and derived_by_node.\nThe only binding removal today is unregister_node (binding.rs:661, free fn\n916), called from remove_subtree_nodes alone.\n\nProposed (about 100-130 lines in reactive.rs and binding.rs):\n- ReactiveGraph::dispose_signal / dispose_derived, modelled on\n  dispose_effect: remove the slot, strip the id from its subscribers'\n  dependencies (signal) or from its dependencies' subscribers (derived),\n  and from tracking / derived_dirty_buffer.\n- Public free functions on the global graph. Effects and computes run with\n  the graph mutex held and IN_FLIGHT_GRAPH set, and their raw closure\n  pointers would dangle if their own node went, so when is_in_flush() is\n  true the call goes onto DEFERRED_WRITES instead. Note DEFERRED_WRITES\n  drains only on Signal::set / set_rebuild / update / update_rebuild and\n  effect(), not on State::set or Computed::try_get.\n- A dispose notifier (same pattern as set_property_binding_notifier, 981)\n  that blinc_layout installs in the REGISTRY initializer (777-795), calling\n  new unregister_signal / unregister_derived on the registry. Release the\n  graph lock before taking the registry's: the registry is locked first on\n  the fire path (binding.rs:782-783 -\u003e read closure -\u003e reactive.rs:1531).\n\nSafe for stale handles: slotmap keys are versioned (as_ffi keeps the\nversion), so a handle to a disposed slot reads None rather than aliasing a\nreused slot. Computed::get panics on None (1536-1539); callers that may hold\na disposed computed should use try_get.\n\nKeyed hooks: disposing a signal still named in HookState.signals would make\nuse_fsm_keyed unwrap None (stateful.rs:1832).","files":null}]}